  "evidence_boundary": "R106 compares frozen A with trainable B native encoders under the same final original selector supervision. Both start from identical complete fresh R84 seed2 selector tensors, three projections and original R102B pretrained ELG/MatNet/ReLD weights. Native pretraining is not selector continuation; its data/overlap remains unknown. Total tensors are identical at initialization, but trainable freedom and training compute are NOT matched. Native stays eval in both arms; B receives gradients from update1 with effective LR0.1 times the common warmup/cosine LR. A does not update native parameters. One input-only native graph per microbatch is shared by the original two dropout selector forwards, with the unchanged CE/comparison/risk/R-Drop and real-row normalization. No auxiliary head or target. All TRAIN/VAL/TEST/LIB calls use online native encoders, never native-feature cache substitution. Native FP32 output precedes normal fusion/selector precision. Raw node4/joint2, physical TSP node0 role, methodID+hand34 and score MLP/maximin remain. Padding-adapted native execution is shared across arms; numerical fixture agreement is not bitwise equivalence or efficacy. Native/FP64 ind, legal-pool Oracle, full-TRAIN SBS; ALL is equal-task macro, mixed raw cost descriptive only. The fixed R84 target36 reports true rescues/losses, false picks and aligned net cost, not choice frequency as recovery. R94B and completed R102B recovery report view are historical, NOT newly matched controls; external pretraining and historical compute are not controlled. Development-exposed TEST; one whole18 minimum-VAL/first-tie checkpoint per arm, no TEST/LIB reselection or per-problem assembly. Actual all18 online native+selector timing is GPU-resident batch128 amortized, NOT singleton or I/O-inclusive end-to-end. Dataset I/O, CPU transfer, training and solver decoding/execution are excluded. Gradient/state witnesses are implementation checks, not selection-effectiveness evidence.",
